# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provokes the enemy picked before onto the one picked now, when several are pulled.
# Switching targets is the whole input: the enemy before the switch becomes the partner,
# and while both stay alive and near they are provoked onto each other, again whenever
# it lapses. The spells and the other bard skills stay on the enemy picked last. With
# four pulled, A to B provokes A onto B, C finds B taken and gets Peace, D provokes C.
# There is no search for a partner: Razor has no expression that finds an enemy, and the
# Next Monster Target hotkeys move lasttarget, which fight/target would take for a pick.
#
# @ hotkeys Cancel Current Target
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ config
#
#   config__use_provo
#      1 provokes the enemy picked before onto the one picked now. 0 never provokes.
#      Both have to be inside config__target_range, the reach of every bard skill here.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__use_provo 1


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ wait
#
#   interval__provo_seen
#      How long the labels are left unread once one has shown provoked or a barding
#      break, the same two seconds as bard/peace.
#
#   interval__provo_retry
#      How long a provocation that failed, or could not reach the pair, waits before the
#      next try. Five seconds is the skill cooldown after a failure (wiki, Bard Necro
#      part 2).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! interval__provo_seen 2000
@setvar! interval__provo_retry 5000


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ timer
#
#   timer__provo_seen, timer__provo_retry
#      Ready on the first pass.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
timer__provo_seen interval__provo_seen
timer__provo_retry interval__provo_retry


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ state
#
#   var__provo_partner
#      The enemy picked before the current one, provoked onto it. 0 when none.
#
#   var__provo_last_target
#      The combat target as this block saw it on the pass before, to notice a switch.
#
#   var__provo_answer
#      Scratch: what the server answered, 0 nothing yet, 1 provoked, 2 try again later,
#      3 the partner cannot be provoked.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! var__provo_partner 0
@setvar! var__provo_last_target 0
@setvar! var__provo_answer 0


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ loop
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # PROVOKE
    #
    # Runs on every pass, outside the fight group, so a switch is noticed even when the
    # new enemy is still out of reach. A switch from one enemy to another makes the one
    # before the partner. When the combat target drops to none, say its partner killed
    # it, the partner is kept, and the next pick gets it: a provoked creature that won
    # its fight is turned on the next enemy.
    #
    # Peace and Provocation share one server slot (Bard Necro part 2), so this goes
    # before bard/peace in the pass and takes the slot whenever a pair can be provoked.
    # bard/peace leaves a provoked target alone. Ensemble still counts it: its condition
    # is Discord and Peace or Provocation.
    #
    # The partner is targeted first and the combat target last, so lasttarget ends on
    # the combat target. A partner the server refuses at the first cursor, out of sight
    # say, would leave lasttarget on it, so it goes into var__target_hold first and no
    # block takes it for a pick. The answers are the lines other Outlands bard scripts
    # read, and the success line also raises the peace/provo bar and the profile's
    # [ provo, target ] overhead.
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    if var__combat_target != var__provo_last_target
        if var__provo_last_target != 0 and var__combat_target != 0
            @setvar! var__provo_partner var__provo_last_target
        endif
        @setvar! var__provo_last_target var__combat_target
    endif

    if config__use_provo = 1 and var__fighting = 1 and var__provo_partner != 0 and var__provo_partner != var__combat_target and timer "timer__provo_seen" >= interval__provo_seen and timer "timer__provo_retry" >= interval__provo_retry and cooldown "peace/provo" = 0 and cooldown "music" = 0 and skill "Provocation" > 0 and not warmode and var__instrument_ok = 1 and var__my_instrument != 0 and not targetexists and not casting
        if find var__provo_partner ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__provo_partner
            if dead alias__provo_partner
                @setvar! var__provo_partner 0
            elseif find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__provo_target
                getlabel alias__provo_partner label__provo_partner
                getlabel alias__provo_target label__provo_target

                if "provoked" in label__provo_partner or "barding break" in label__provo_partner or "provoked" in label__provo_target or "barding break" in label__provo_target
                    settimer "timer__provo_seen" 0
                else
                    useskill 'Provocation'
                    waitfortarget wait__bard_target

                    # Answered once, the way bard/peace does.
                    if insysmsg "What instrument shall you play"
                        target var__my_instrument
                        waitfortarget wait__bard_target

                        if insysmsg "That is not a musical instrument"
                            @setvar! var__my_instrument 0
                        endif
                    endif

                    if targetexists
                        @setvar! var__target_hold var__provo_partner
                        target alias__provo_partner
                        waitfortarget wait__bard_target
                    endif

                    if targetexists
                        target alias__provo_target
                        wait wait__short
                    endif

                    if targetexists
                        hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                        wait wait__short
                    endif

                    # The answer comes within a second. Read on every round until it
                    # does, with no break: this loop sits inside the main one.
                    @setvar! var__provo_answer 0
                    for 5
                        if var__provo_answer = 0
                            if insysmsg "play successfully, provoking"
                                @setvar! var__provo_answer 1
                            elseif insysmsg "You fail to incite" or insysmsg "too far away" or insysmsg "Target cannot be seen" or insysmsg "You must wait a few moments"
                                @setvar! var__provo_answer 2
                            elseif insysmsg "incite that"
                                @setvar! var__provo_answer 3
                            else
                                wait wait__short
                            endif
                        endif
                    endfor

                    if var__provo_answer = 1
                        settimer "timer__provo_seen" 0
                    elseif var__provo_answer = 2
                        settimer "timer__provo_retry" 0
                    elseif var__provo_answer = 3
                        @setvar! var__provo_partner 0
                        if config__chatty = 1
                            overhead "[ provo, wrong ]" 254
                        endif
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        elseif not find var__provo_partner ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range
            # Gone, or too far to come back into the fight.
            @setvar! var__provo_partner 0
        endif
    endif
